// EXPECT: argument 'n' of 'take' narrows word to int; declare a int local and pass that
// IDCPY-ACCEPTS
// docs/FRICTION.md 12. idc.py has no rule against this: it compiles the
// program and prints the truncated value. The marker asserts that, so the day
// idc.py grows the rule this case fails and gets updated.
main() {
  word a = 4294967297;
  take(a);
} return int 0;

take(int n) {
  print(n);
} return void;
